  "explanations": [
    ]
}

{
  "recap": "Beyond maximizing total importance, we must also account for waiting time, which is the maximum time a user needs to inspect or interact with an object at a specific point of interest. This waiting time is defined as a function for each node, mapping it to a positive real number. Similar to total importance, the total waiting time for any given path is calculated by summing the individual waiting times of all the nodes in that path.",
  "explanations": [
    ]
  }

{
  "recap": "Perception occurs when real-time sensory signals are combined with knowledge stored in long-term memory within the cerebral cortex. This combination allows us to interpret stimuli, such as recognizing a face or identifying music, rather than just receiving raw data. Therefore, how we perceive something depends heavily on our prior life experience and knowledge.",
